#N canvas 20 20 3000 2700 12;
#X text 20 20 c_presence -- one device's last-heard clock. It counts ticks since its device last spoke and declares it lost past a threshold \, on presence and on err. One inside each m_ layer that can be polled., f 84;
#X text 20 190 creation arg 1: the SOURCE NAME \, which is the abstraction's own name -- m_nano \, never nanoKONTROL. REQUIRED. creation arg 2: how many missed ticks count as lost. creation arg 3: the STAGGER in ms \, see below. inlet 1: SEEN -- send it anything at all whenever your device speaks. outlet 1: a bang meaning POLL YOUR DEVICE NOW. outlet 2: presence \, 1 or 0 \, on the transition only., f 84;
#X text 20 370 The source is the abstraction's name \, never the device's: that is the m_ boundary \, and err's source field already carries the same names., f 84;
#X text 20 550 Only pollable devices get one \, because a passive device must not age: mother pushes the Organelle's knobs once at load (item 237) \, so an aging m_organelle would be lost a few seconds into every boot., f 84;
#X text 20 780 The stagger keeps the inquiries apart: one tick reaches every instance at once \, and replies interleaved byte by byte on the one [sysexin] would corrupt c_devid's count., f 84;
#X text 20 980 The counter is re-evaluated from two places that meet at the >=: seen sends a literal 0 through the test \, so a device that comes back is back at once rather than at the next tick., f 84;
#X text 20 1150 change is bare on purpose: it starts holding 0 \, and 0 is not-lost \, so nothing is published until something crosses., f 84;
